  "description": "An otherwise-clean linear scan with one dust-speck/artifact patch: patch 50 (which should read ~127 on the ramp) is corrupted to a clipped 0. FINDING, not a bug in this port -- a faithfully-preserved fragility in the original algorithm, made concrete by this fixture: the clipped patch becomes the new recorded compute_dynamic_range minimum (0, at index 50), which breaks the monotonic-descending-samples assumption find_value_for relies on. The pipeline does NOT error (verify_curve only checks x-values, which are untouched) -- it silently returns a curve where x=0.0 drops out entirely and the y-values for roughly the first half of the range (x=20..118) collapse to a narrow, substantively wrong band clustered around 128, instead of tracking x as the clean scan does. This fixture exists specifically to pin that distorted-but-not-erroring behavior, not to claim the algorithm handles a single bad patch gracefully.",
